@startuml SensibLawGovernanceComplianceTOE
title SensibLaw governance and compliance firewalls at DASHI TOE

skinparam componentStyle rectangle

package "Canonical #1323 governance facade" {
  [SensibLawGovernanceTOEExact] as Governance
}

package "Existing source-owned compliance proofs" {
  [ExpertEvidenceProductionIntegrity] as Expert
  [RealMatterReviewDecision] as Review
  [LegalSemanticAdmissionFrontier] as Admission
  [PromotionSpine] as Promotion
  [LegalDecisionDoubleProjection] as LegalDecision
  [LegitimacyEvidenceSeparation] as Legitimacy
  [FleetFormalGapTargetTOEExact] as Fleet
}

package "Thin extension" {
  [SensibLawGovernanceComplianceTOEExact] as Compliance
  [SensibLawGovernanceComplianceTOEValidation] as Validation
}

package "TOE roots" {
  [EverythingTOESymmetryResolved369] as TOE
  [Unifier] as Unifier
  [Unified.Everything] as Unified
}

Governance --> Compliance : vendor-neutral governance
Expert --> Compliance : qualification != forensic compliance
Review --> Compliance : review != applicability or truth
Admission --> Compliance : candidate != admission authority
Promotion --> Compliance : missing gates -> abstain
LegalDecision --> Compliance : official surface loses fine state
Legitimacy --> Compliance : legality != legitimacy
Fleet --> Compliance : target 58 only
584 discharged, 44 separate

Compliance --> TOE
Compliance --> Unifier
Compliance --> Validation
TOE --> Validation
Unifier --> Validation
Compliance --> Unified
Validation --> Unified

note right of Governance
Actionstep is not a theorem owner here.
Vendor identity does not create authority.
A target domain needs its own authority witness.
end note

note bottom of Fleet
The external fleet receipt is scheduling context.
Eigenvalue magnitude and external counts do not create proof.
Independent equal cardinalities do not create same-object identity.
end note

note left of Compliance
O: close the missing compliance firewall seam
R: reuse #1323 and canonical proof owners
C: add one receipt and facade aliases
S: preserve non-promotion and non-factorability
L: one disjoint legal-compliance lane
P: current owners exist; ESD stays read-only
G: standards are process lenses, not certification
F: exact-owner validation, trust scan, ESD scan, referee/preflight
end note

@enduml
